Access to your filesystem, I do not have. To list folders larger than 2 GB, run:

```bash
du -sk /Users/albou/tmp/abstractframework/untracked/* 2>/dev/null | awk '$1 > 2097152 { printf "%.2f GB\t%s\n", $1/1048576, $2 }' | sort -hr
```

For nested folders too, use:

```bash
find /Users/albou/tmp/abstractframework/untracked -type d -exec du -sk {} + 2>/dev/null | awk '$1 > 2097152 { printf "%.2f GB\t%s\n", $1/1048576, $2 }' | sort -hr
```